      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "7ba39eb62eed6fbcdfea186f793de4e46b7ece2d",
            "subject": "LU-17240 tests: unmount targets in parallel"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-13 08:55:51.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-13 08:55:51.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-17240 tests: start targets through shared start_facets()",
        "message": "LU-17240 tests: start targets through shared start_facets()\n\nmountmds() and mountoss() each have their own loop to start targets\nin parallel, and conf-sanity needs a third copy for its MDTs.\n\nAdd start_facets(), the counterpart of unmount_facets(), to start a\nlist of targets through start() with their usual devices and mount\noptions, plus any options given.  The MGS and MDT0000 start first,\nand the other targets after them, in parallel if enabled for their\ntype.  With --skip-mounted, a target that is already mounted only\nhas its variables set, as mountmds() and mountoss() did.\nmountmgs(), mountmds() and mountoss() now use it.  This changes no\ntimings by itself; it lets conf-sanity use the same parallel start\ninstead of a copy of it (next patch).  It is not\nmount_facets(), which remounts targets after a failover with the\ndevice and options of their last start().\n\nIf MDT0000 fails to start, mountmds() now returns without starting\nthe other MDTs, instead of trying them anyway.  Every caller fails\nthe test on that error.\n\nunmount_facets() now also takes a comma-separated list, as\nget_facets() prints it, and removes $TMP/mgsactive along with\n$TMP/mds1active when the MGS is combined with MDT0000, which\nstopall() did itself before.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: mdtcount=4 mdscount=2 testlist=sanity\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I369406314bcf4441c9f0c45bc07307da91f37671\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
